Dynamons microG Launcher 0.5.0 - page-first account runtime

Install this APK over the existing microG probe. Do not uninstall or clear data.
Host: com.dynamongamer.microgprobe; version code 8; ARM64; min SDK 26.
Original game: com.funtomic.dynamons3, publisher-signed installed base and splits.
The original game is never rebuilt, re-signed or replaced. Existing container
account/game data directories are retained by in-place runtime import.

One APK now contains the modified account-services runtime. Tap Prepare & sign in,
then tap Sign in on its consent screen. Google login opens through the runtime's
real Google HTTPS WebView. The official microG Companion is reused if its verified
file is cached, otherwise a 4.2 MB official Companion download is needed.
After completing actual Google authentication, use Run full startup test and the
game's own sign-in button. Adding an account is not Play Games authentication.

Runtime changes from MorpheApp/MicroG-RE tag 7.2.1:
- Uses com.google.android.gms and account type com.google so the original game
  and installed account data need no package-name modifications.
- Loads Google's genuine EmbeddedSetup page BEFORE initial device check-in.
- Reveals a completed secure accounts.google.com page without relying solely
  on Google's page-specific JavaScript visibility callback.
- Cookie clearing: 10-second deadline. Initial-page load: 45-second deadline.
  Main-frame network/HTTP errors show an error; failed pages are not revealed.
- Authentication, registration and profile requests have 15-second connect and
  20-second read deadlines. Optional profile lookup/registration run after the
  authenticated account-token response and do not hold the success screen.
- Empty master/account-token responses are rejected. No fabricated successful
  account, token, network or Play Games result is returned.
- Full authentication request/response and navigation URL debug logging removed
  from the changed paths. Host diagnostics never read credentials or cookies.
- Upstream automatic/manual installer update paths disabled: upstream app.revanced
  APKs cannot update this standard-namespace custom runtime. Host pins exact bytes.
- Custom label/icon/version; upstream licenses/attribution included in source.

This runtime is OUR modified source-built fork, not an official Morphe/Google APK.
Source: https://github.com/MorpheApp/MicroG-RE/tree/7.2.1 (Apache-2.0).
Runtime version: 7.2.1-dynamons1 / 255070218; ARM64-only; non-debuggable release.
Runtime size: 44666034 bytes.
Runtime SHA-256: 5e7bed9c17b9fb27a23902b685ef44968019c31287fb1203ac6d41e0205d02bb
Companion: official microG com.android.vending 84022634 / 0.3.17.40226.
Companion SHA-256: 9b8616011cc8f026bcbbe094df850794abb9d6d9f23214d7a8f8c4d1033ea012
Guest service compatibility is limited to exact pinned runtime/Companion APKs.
It does not change the game's certificate or grant OS privileged permissions.
Phone Google APKs, outside-phone account sessions, tokens and passwords are not copied.

Verification performed in this workspace:
- Modified runtime ARM64 release build and launcher build succeeded.
- 99 host regression scenarios and 20 login URL/timeout policy checks passed.
- Actual packaged runtime DEX inspected: real Google URL, page-before-checkin,
  bounded transport/cookie/page waits, error handling, standard account type and
  background post-login registration are present in 23 inspected classes.
- All host DEX files checked; bundled runtime hash and new installation path present.
- APK signatures, ZIP CRC, package/version, ABI and alignment verified.
- Bundled runtime bytes match the exact pinned hash/size.
- Launcher signing certificate matches the previous update; engine native library
  bytes are unchanged from the game-working 0.4.0 host.
- Anonymous network check of Google's EmbeddedSetup endpoint returned HTTP 200
  with sign-in form content and no browser-rejection marker. No account was used.

Not verified: Android installation, visible login-page rendering on the phone,
actual Google authentication, Play Games sign-in or cloud-save restoration.
No Android device/emulator was attached here. An HTTP response/code inspection is
not an Android runtime test. This is an experimental APK, not guaranteed login.

Complete source ZIP contains launcher/ and account-runtime/ source trees,
licenses, tests and the signed bundled runtime asset. Private signing keys,
build caches, local SDK paths and generated build outputs are excluded.
